<title>HONG KONG: Sino Land, Varitronix up after MSCI move.</title>
<headline>Sino Land, Varitronix up after MSCI move.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sino Land Co Ltd and Varitronix International Ltd surged on Thursday after Morgan Stanley Capital Index (MSCI) said it would include the stocks in its indices effective May 30, brokers said.</p>
<p>The changes were part of a shuffle of Asian stocks in MSCI's indices.</p>
<p>Sino Land finished the session HK$0.65 higher at HK$8.00. Brokers said the stock had lagged a recent market rise and had attracted bargain hunters.</p>
<p>Varitronix, a liquid crystal display maker and designer, surged HK$1.25 to HK$12.05.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6369</p>
